WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.280
Since its announcement, Hulu's biopic "Pam&nbsp;
&amp; Tommy" has been wrapped up in controversy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.840
The series depicts a more idealistic time in&nbsp;
the mid '90s when celebrity sex tapes were not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.800
as frequent as they have come to be. This caused a&nbsp;
perfect storm for Pamela Anderson, played by Lily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.200
James and Tommy Lee played by Sebastian Stan,&nbsp;
when their private honeymoon video was stolen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.760
from their home. Many have come out against even&nbsp;
the idea of such a series portraying this story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.840
The notorious singer for the grunge band Hole,&nbsp;
Courtney Love, defended Anderson's right to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.040
privacy. She said in a statement "My heart goes&nbsp;
out to Pammy further causing her complex trauma".

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.160
Love's statement refers to how Anderson&nbsp;
was treated by the press at the time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.320
She was publicly shamed by many outlets, and&nbsp;
according to Entertainment Weekly, she refuses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.960
to ever watch the show. The new Hulu series&nbsp;
is from "I, Tonya" director Craig Gillespie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.360
who was also criticized for his sympathetic&nbsp;
portrayal of Tonya Harding in his previous film.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.320
In addition to these factors,&nbsp;
there is one former band member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.840
that has some strong opinions about&nbsp;
Lee's portrayal in "Pam &amp; Tommy."

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.640
Formed in 1981, Mötley Crüe was a hair metal&nbsp;
band that quickly became known for their antics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.040
One of their most famous anecdotes is the time&nbsp;
Ozzy Osbourne snorted a line of ants, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.760
detailed in the band's memoir and film of the same&nbsp;
name, "The Dirt". What may be lesser-known is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:14.560
brief period of time when frontman Vince Neil left&nbsp;
the band, which is not portrayed in "Pam &amp; Tommy."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.440
In 1992, Neil was replaced with John Corabi,&nbsp;
who performed with the band for five years.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.680
Corabi sang on the band's self-titled album&nbsp;
in 1994, and did not continue when Neil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.800
returned for the comeback album in 1997. For&nbsp;
Sebastian Stan's transformation into Tommy Lee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.040
the actor reached out, and Lee officially gave&nbsp;
his blessing to "Pam &amp; Tommy." Despite this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.360
Corabi does not agree with how Lee is portrayed&nbsp;
in the limited series. In a powerful statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.440
on his social media, Corabi defended many&nbsp;
players who this real-life story touched.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.120
On his Twitter account, Corabi published a&nbsp;
lengthy statement in defense of the real-life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.960
people who were involved in the story behind&nbsp;
"Pam &amp; Tommy." The singer was adamant that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.800
the character of Lee in the show is a work&nbsp;
of fiction, and not relevant to reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.080
Corabi wrote in his statement, "I shared&nbsp;
5 years of my life with Tommy,[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.800
And although at times it was INSANITY it's&nbsp;
sooooo overblown." The singer went on to explain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.720
that these events were sensationalized&nbsp;
for what "they call tv entertainment."

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:08.800
In the show, Lee is often demonstrated&nbsp;
as being outrageous and oftentimes cruel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.720
The main catalyst for the aforementioned break-in&nbsp;
and subsequent theft of Anderson and Lee's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.040
sex tape was because of Lee's treatment&nbsp;
of his former carpenter Rand Gauthier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.440
Gauthier expected to be paid for materials&nbsp;
and to retrieve his tools from Lee's property.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.280
Instead, Lee met him with a shotgun and&nbsp;
refused to pay him. Later in the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.560
Anderson is shocked to hear that Lee&nbsp;
refused to pay for services rendered.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.040
Corabi's defense isn't just extended to Lee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.840
There is another significant&nbsp;
person who he goes to the mat for.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.480
Pamela Anderson was a sad footnote at the time&nbsp;
of this scandal. As portrayed in "Pam &amp; Tommy,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.400
Anderson had to face the brunt of abuse from&nbsp;
comedians like Jay Leno, while Lee was often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.120
let off easily from the limelight. Corabi has&nbsp;
come to her defense in light of this trauma, too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.720
He wrote on Twitter: "Apparently HULU, and&nbsp;
all involved in this crock of s*** don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.640
care about how Pam may feel to have to&nbsp;
relive this". His concern also extended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.120
to Anderson and Lee's two sons who they continue&nbsp;
to co-parent, despite the end of their marriage.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.400
There are elements of Anderson's life&nbsp;
that are not in Corabi's statement and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.040
are entirely glossed over in "Pam &amp; Tommy"&nbsp;
as well. As Showbiz CheatSheet states,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.840
the couple briefly reconciled after Lee's spent&nbsp;
time in prison due to spousal abuse. The Hulu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.320
series mentions the domestic violence in Anderson&nbsp;
and Lee's relationship briefly in the end credits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:21.120
but did not make that a priority in the series,&nbsp;
nor did Corabi mention it in his Twitter post.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.000
Anderson has been through many trials&nbsp;
because of this time in her life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.040
and continues to stick by her decision&nbsp;
not to be involved with the show.

